{% comment %}
  A certification row: image, feature list, price, buy button.

  One section for the mockup's .certrow AND .bundle -- the same shape, differing
  only in surface, column ratio and crop. The bundle is this with `dark` on.

  ORDER. Markup is always text-then-image; the visual swap is CSS `order`, so
  reading and tab order stay correct. Below 1020px the image always follows the
  text.

  CHECKOUT. `go_to_checkout` posts a return_to of /checkout, so the buyer lands
  on checkout rather than the cart. The mockup specifies this for these items
  ("Straight to secure checkout") and it suits them: single high-value
  purchases with nothing to cross-sell alongside. It is the wrong default for
  small items on a page that sells two things -- see the study guides, which
  deliberately go to cart.

  FEATURES are blocks so the list can change without a developer. They are the
  substance of the offer and they churn.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign classes = 'suf-cert'
  if section.settings.dark
    assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-cert--dark'
    if section.settings.flush_top
      assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-cert--flush-top'
    endif
  else
    assign classes = 'suf-section ' | append: classes
  endif

  assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-cert--image-' | append: section.settings.image_side

  if section.settings.frame != 'none'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-cert--frame-' | append: section.settings.frame
  endif

  assign product = section.settings.product
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor | handle
-%}

<div class="{{ classes }}" {% if anchor != blank %}id="{{ anchor }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    <div class="suf-cert__inner">
      <div class="suf-cert__text">
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="suf-eyebrow{% if section.settings.dark %} suf-eyebrow--on-dark{% endif %}">
            {%- render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.eyebrow -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          {%- if section.settings.dark -%}
            <h2>{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.heading %}</h2>
          {%- else -%}
            <h3>{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.heading %}</h3>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
          <div class="suf-cert__lead">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.body %}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
          <ul class="suf-whylist{% if section.settings.dark %} suf-whylist--on-dark{% endif %}">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
                <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{% render 'suf-nb', text: block.settings.text %}</li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if product != blank -%}
          <p class="suf-pricerow">
            <span class="suf-pricerow__price">{{ product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
            {%- if section.settings.compare_note != blank -%}
              <span class="suf-pricerow__was">{{ section.settings.compare_note | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>

          {%- if product.available -%}
            {%- form 'product', product, class: 'suf-cert__form' -%}
              <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
              {%- if section.settings.go_to_checkout -%}
                <input type="hidden" name="return_to" value="/checkout">
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- comment -%}
                SEMINAR CREDIT. Optional by design -- see the snippet for why
                the default is "choose later".

                A line item PROPERTY rather than a variant: every combination
                costs the same, and variants exist to vary price, inventory or
                SKU. Putting a running list of seminars into variants would
                also mean editing this product every time one is added or
                retired, which is the maintenance this avoids.

                The property is named "Seminar" so it reads as itself in the
                cart, on the order and in the admin -- that is where staff pick
                it up to enrol someone.

                An EMPTY value is meaningful, not missing: it records "to be
                scheduled". Shopify hides properties with a blank value from
                the cart, which is the behaviour we want -- someone who has not
                chosen sees no half-answered line.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                WHAT THE BUYER IS CHOOSING, for a bundle that is "any two of
                three". One option per line in a textarea; a line ending in
                `|seminar` marks a combination that includes one, which is what
                reveals the seminar picker below.

                A PROPERTY, NOT VARIANTS. Every combination costs $XXX, and
                variants exist to vary price, inventory or SKU. Variants would
                also mean the merchant maintaining a matrix in admin for
                something that is really one question with three answers.

                The pipe convention matches the list blocks in suf-legal, so a
                merchant meets the same idea twice rather than two syntaxes.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign picks = section.settings.picks | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
              {%- if section.settings.picks != blank -%}
                <div class="suf-cert__picks">
                  <label for="suf-picks-{{ section.id }}">
                    {{- section.settings.picks_label | default: 'Your two' | escape -}}
                  </label>
                  <select id="suf-picks-{{ section.id }}" name="properties[Selection]" data-suf-picks>
                    {%- for line in picks -%}
                      {%- assign clean = line | strip -%}
                      {%- if clean != blank -%}
                        {%- assign has_seminar = false -%}
                        {%- if clean contains '|seminar' -%}
                          {%- assign has_seminar = true -%}
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {%- assign text = clean | split: '|' | first | strip -%}
                        <option value="{{ text | escape }}" data-seminar="{{ has_seminar }}">
                          {{- text -}}
                        </option>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- comment -%}
                RENDERED VISIBLE, HIDDEN BY SCRIPT. assets/suf-bundle.js hides
                this when the chosen combination has no seminar in it, and
                disables the select so a stale value cannot ride along on an
                order it does not belong to.

                Written this way round on purpose: with no JavaScript the field
                simply shows, and someone can still say which seminar they
                want. Hiding it in markup and revealing it with script would
                mean a failed asset silently removes the choice. Same reasoning
                as the [data-suf-motion] gate in _suf-motion.scss.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if section.settings.seminar_credit and section.settings.events_collection != blank -%}
                <div class="suf-cert__seminar" data-suf-seminar-field>
                  <label for="suf-seminar-{{ section.id }}">
                    {{- section.settings.seminar_label | default: 'Your seminar' | escape -}}
                  </label>
                  <select id="suf-seminar-{{ section.id }}" name="properties[Seminar]">
                    {%- render 'suf-seminar-options', events: section.settings.events_collection -%}
                  </select>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
              <button type="submit" class="suf-btn suf-btn--primary" name="add">
                {{- section.settings.button_label | default: 'Buy Now' | escape -}}
              </button>
            {%- endform -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <p class="suf-btn-micro">Currently unavailable.</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.micro != blank -%}
          <div class="suf-btn-micro">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.micro %}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
        <div class="suf-cert__media">
          {{
            section.settings.image
            | image_url: width: 900
            | image_tag:
              loading: 'lazy',
              widths: '440, 600, 900',
              sizes: '(min-width: 1021px) 40vw, 90vw',
              alt: section.settings.image_alt
          }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.pointer != blank -%}
      <div class="suf-cert__pointer">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.pointer %}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Certification row (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 10,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow" },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Lead paragraph" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor",
      "label": "Anchor id",
      "info": "Lets a button elsewhere link to this row, e.g. \"bundle\" for #bundle."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Product" },
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "product",
      "label": "Product",
      "info": "Price and availability come from this. The row does not link to the product page -- it sells in place."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Buy Now" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "go_to_checkout",
      "label": "Go straight to checkout",
      "info": "Skips the cart. Right for a single high-value purchase; wrong on a page that sells more than one thing, where it kills the second sale.",
      "default": false
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "What the buyer chooses" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "picks",
      "label": "Combinations",
      "info": "One per line, for a bundle that is \"any two of three\". End a line with |seminar to mark a combination that includes a seminar -- that is what reveals the seminar picker. Leave empty if there is nothing to choose."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "picks_label",
      "label": "Combinations label",
      "default": "Your two"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Seminar credit" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "seminar_credit",
      "label": "Includes a seminar",
      "info": "Adds an OPTIONAL seminar picker above the button, defaulting to \"I'll choose later\". The seminar is sold as a credit and booked afterwards -- asking someone to commit to a travel date at checkout costs conversions and cannot be answered at all for a package carrying several. Needs the collection below.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "events_collection",
      "label": "Seminars collection",
      "info": "Past seminars are dropped automatically, on the same end-date rule the seminars page uses."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "seminar_label",
      "label": "Picker label",
      "default": "Your seminar"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "compare_note",
      "label": "Price comparison",
      "info": "Sits beside the price, e.g. \"$X,XXX bought separately\"."
    },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "micro", "label": "Fine print under the button" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Image" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Image alt text" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_side",
      "label": "Image side",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "Right" }
      ],
      "default": "left"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "frame",
      "label": "Offset frame",
      "info": "BLUE when the image is on the left, RED when it is on the right. Follow the image side, not the section above -- that is the convention across the site.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "red", "label": "Red" },
        { "value": "blue", "label": "Blue" },
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" }
      ],
      "default": "red"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Surface" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "dark",
      "label": "Dark band",
      "info": "Full-bleed navy, square crop, larger heading. Count the dark bands already on the page first.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "flush_top",
      "label": "Butt against the band above",
      "info": "Dark bands only. Zeroes this band's top margin and adds a hairline seam, so two navy bands read as one block. The band above needs its own \"Butt against the band below\".",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "pointer",
      "label": "Closing note",
      "info": "Centred line under the row, for a route out to a bigger package."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "feature",
      "name": "Feature",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "inline_richtext",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Feature",
          "info": "Bold the first few words -- the list is scanned, not read."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Certification row (SUF)",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "feature" }, { "type": "feature" }, { "type": "feature" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
